  "behavior": [
    "Native AllocateOptimal returns immediately after a successful enabled fast bump: it does not move a nearly-full block into myUsedHeap or repair decreasing-availability order. Existing Rust code ignored the flag and always reordered.",
    "IncEngine now records the requested native policy. Allocations already fitting the head skip reorder only while enabled; new-block slow paths still reorder. Allocate and AllocateOptimal share this path as upstream does.",
    "Mode toggles do not reorder or reset blocks. Reset(false) rewinds in creation-reverse order while preserving mode; Reset(true) restores default block size but preserves mode.",
    "The existing Rust Mutex still covers either policy. Allocation and typed/raw-owner lease acquisition retain their existing single critical section; f51a93dc allocation/reset race correction is unchanged.",
    "Seven focused tests cover 11 exact native rows and live typed-owner preservation. Replacing the corrected production files with unchanged base files made five focused regressions fail (two remain green); retained baseline log records this controlled comparison."
  ],
