  "adaptations_and_remaining_gaps": [
    "Rust always serializes allocator state with a Mutex. It reproduces measured successful single-thread allocation/list histories, not native shared-lock/CAS performance, lock-free progress or all concurrent scheduling outcomes. Toggling concurrently is safely serialized although native documents that domain as undefined.",
    "IncBlock remains a scalar bookkeeping adapter rather than the public native atomic IBlock object; intrusive header layout, raw fields, protected allocateSlow/resetBlock/clean/increaseBlockSize callable access and custom allocator virtual override hooks are not closed by this change.",
    "Typed allocation alignment, raw heap reservation headers, live-lease Reset rejection, allocation failure reporting and requests that native truncates beyond u32 retain existing Rust safety differences. No exact physical heap footprint or arbitrary allocator-hook equivalence is claimed.",
    "CellFilter core supported methods have concrete adapters, but signed negative dimension construction, invalid/nonfinite coordinate casts, dimension/size mismatches and zero-dimensional range traversal do not claim native equivalence. Native signed dimension underflow/allocation domains are not expanded by this slice.",
    "CellFilter raw protected fields and mutable object links are not public writable equivalents. Implicit whole-filter special members and arbitrary downstream subclasses are outside the explicit declaration checklist.",
    "CellIndex LP64 size/alignment/offsets match measured native storage, but inline pointer slot stores None rather than a self-reference. Public generic LocalArray storage, generic payload ABI and external byte inspection remain partial.",
    "Native Cell move assignment discards old targets without destruction; explicit Rust discard adapters preserve that defined behavior but allocator lease cleanup and panic recovery adaptations remain documented in cell-filter-cell-methods/native-engine receipts. Range iteration may make extra private index copies; allocation callback/global heap byte observations remain partial.",
    "All nine original CellFilter tests remain green. Declaration-to-adapter joins provide navigation and bounded evidence, not automatic global API/body proof or full kernel parity."
  ]
